        "prop": "spectrum",
        "displayScale": 1.05
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e16",
      "type": "textlabel",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 150,
      "params": {
        "text": "1 — The seed leaves the laser at its 31 fs limit. The stretcher (+100 000 fs²) spreads its colours over ~9 ps, red first.",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "fill": "#276aa2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e17",
      "type": "textlabel",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 175,
      "params": {
        "text": "2 — The OPA amplifies each colour with the pump intensity it meets at that moment: the 12 ps pump and saturation shape the amplified band.",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "fill": "#8f2d2d"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e18",
      "type": "textlabel",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 200,
      "params": {
        "text": "3 — The signal keeps the seed's chirp, so the compressor (−100 000 fs²) recompresses it; idler and residual pump are dumped.",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "fill": "#1f7a4d"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e19",
      "type": "textlabel",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 540,
      "params": {
        "text": "Try: shorten the pump, delay it (pulse phase), or remove the stretcher — the probes and the OPA readout show the amplified band and duration follow.",
        "fontSize": 12,
        "fill": "#555555"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e20",
      "type": "textlabel",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 565,
      "params": {
        "text": "Model boundary: gain from the data-sheet settings (no crystal, phase matching or walk-off); the signal keeps the seed's phase only where the pump gates slowly — the OPA readout says when not.",
        "fontSize": 12,
        "fill": "#555555"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e21",
      "type": "textlabel",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 590,
      "params": {
        "text": "The idler's spectral phase (the conjugate chirp) is not modelled. Idler and residual pump go to beam dumps.",
        "fontSize": 12,
        "fill": "#555555"
      }
    }
  ],
  "beams": []
}
